aperture-plus is an experimental WebKit browser for iOS and macOS with an
embedded userspace Tailscale node, written almost entirely by Avery Pennarun.
Latchkey strips it to a single-purpose client for a self-hosted KiroCrew
dashboard: one window, one destination, no tabs, no address bar, no macOS
target, and no virtualization.

Modifications are copyright (c) 2026 Olof Johansson and are released under the
same BSD 3-Clause License.

It also vendors, as git submodules:

    tailscale/libtailscale   ThirdParty/libtailscale
    tailscale/tailscale      ThirdParty/libtailscale/tailscale-patched (patched)

both BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c) Tailscale Inc & contributors.

Divergences from upstream are recorded in ../docs/DECISIONS.md.
